			  "Agents": {
			    "Internal": {
			      "Version": "1.1.0"
			    }
			  },
			  "CustomInstructions": "\n• Policy sales data comes from fact_policy_sales.\n• Revenue means SUM of premium_amount.\n• Policy count means COUNT of policy_id.\n• Customer refers to dim_customer.\n• Festival refers to dim_festival.\n• Date-based analysis should use dim_date\n\n• fact_policy_sales is the central fact table.\n• All dimensions join to fact_policy_sales using their respective ID columns.\n• Festival-based analysis must use festival_id.\n• Customer-based analysis must use customer_id.\n\n• If no date is specified, assume current calendar year.\n• If no festival is specified, include all festivals.\n• If no region is specified, include all regions.\n\n• \"Top\" or \"highest\" means descending order by revenue.\n• \"Lowest\" or \"least\" means ascending order by revenue.\n• Trend analysis should compare current year with previous year.\n\n• Average premium = total premium_amount divided by policy count.\n• High value customer = customer with total premium_amount greater than 100000 INR.\n\nBusiness Context:\n\n1. fact_policy_sales contains insurance policy sales transactions.\n2. festival_id links fact_policy_sales with dim_festival.\n3. dim_festival contains festival_name and festival_year.\n4. To calculate festival sales, use fact_policy_sales.festival_id.\n5. Do NOT use dim_date to identify festival sales.\n6. Diwali sales comparison should be calculated using festival_year in dim_festival.\n7. Sales revenue is stored in fact_policy_sales.sales_amount.\n8. Profit is stored in fact_policy_sales.profit_amount.\n"
			}
		contentType: json

